        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You generate technical handoffs for Support cases that have already been approved for Engineering escalation.\n\nYour job is NOT to decide whether the case should be escalated. That decision has already been made upstream.\n\nUsing only the evidence provided:\n- summarize the technical issue concisely\n- describe customer impact\n- summarize relevant system evidence\n- include relevant business context\n- explain the correlation between the reported symptoms and system health\n\nDo not invent root causes, logs, incidents, errors, remediation steps, or technical facts that are not present in the input.\n\nKeep the handoff factual, concise, and useful for an engineer starting an investigation.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nUse exactly this structure:\n\n{\n  \"incident_summary\": \"string\",\n  \"customer_impact\": \"string\",\n  \"system_evidence\": \"string\",\n  \"business_context\": \"string\",\n  \"investigation_context\": \"string\"\n}\n\nDo not add markdown, code fences, commentary, or any fields outside this structure."
            },
            {
              "content": "=Create a technical Engineering handoff for this already-approved escalation.\n\nSUPPORT CASE\nTicket title: {{ $json.ticket_title }}\nCustomer message: {{ $json.message }}\n\nCUSTOMER CONTEXT\nCustomer: {{ $json.customer_name }}\nSegment: {{ $json.customer_segment }}\nARR: ${{ $json.arr }}\nSLA: {{ $json.sla }}\nRegion: {{ $json.region }}\n\nSYSTEM EVIDENCE\nAffected service: {{ $json.service }}\nSystem status: {{ $json.status }}\nError rate: {{ $json.error_rate }}\nP95 latency: {{ $json.p95_latency_ms }} ms\nActive incident: {{ $json.active_incident }}\nAffected region: {{ $json.affected_region }}\n\nESCALATION CONTEXT\nDecision source: {{ $json.decision_source }}\nDecision confidence: {{ $json.model_confidence }}\nDecision reason: {{ $json.decision_reason }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
